🧪 What exactly was done in this lab
1. 📥 Loaded sequential dataset
You used multiple sentences (text data)
This is sequential data where order of words matters
Goal: learn patterns in sequences
2. 🔢 Converted text to numbers (Tokenization)
Used Tokenizer
Each word → unique integer
Example:
machine → 1, learning → 2

👉 This makes text usable for neural networks

3. 🔗 Created input-output sequences
Broke each sentence into smaller sequences

Example:
machine learning models
→

machine → learning
machine learning → models

👉 So model learns:
previous words → next word

4. 📏 Applied padding
Made all sequences same length using pad_sequences
Added zeros at beginning

👉 Required for fixed input size in model

5. 🎯 Split into input (X) and output (y)
X = sequence of previous words
y = next word

Example:
X = machine learning
y = models

6. 🔄 Converted output to one-hot encoding
Output word converted into vector form
Used for classification
7. 🤖 Built LSTM model

Model has 3 layers:

Embedding layer → converts numbers to word vectors
LSTM layer → learns sequence patterns and context
Dense layer → predicts next word

👉 This is a sequence-based generative model

8. 🏋️ Trained the model
Used dataset to train model (model.fit)
Model learns word patterns over multiple epochs
9. ✨ Generated new text
Gave input like "machine learning"
Model predicts next word repeatedly
Forms a new sentence

👉 Example output:
machine learning models learn patterns from data

